-- title:
--   Reduced norms of Eichler-order ideles realise all unit ideles
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq 2$, and assume [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87): that is, $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q$ lies in the prime $w$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and $N$ a natural number with [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder R N`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L69), i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ each maximal among orders containing it, with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $\varepsilon=(\varepsilon_w)_w$ assign to each height-one prime $w$ an element of $\mathbb{Q}_w$ of valuation $1$. Then there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ lying in [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) — the stabiliser, for the multiplication action on the ambient ring, of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral — such that for every $w$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w\cong\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{i},z_{j},z_{k})$ coordinatewise, the reduced norm $x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_i^2-bx_j^2+abx_k^2$ of $\varphi$ applied to the $w$-component of $u$ equals $\varepsilon_w$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity of the reduced norm from the unit group of the adelic completion of an Eichler order in a definite rational quaternion algebra onto the group of unit ideles, the global consequence of local norm-maximality of Eichler orders at split and at ramified places. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph, where elements of prescribed local reduced norm (for instance the ramified prime, or a unit at every place) must be produced inside the idelic unit group.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsEichlerOrder_exists_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_forall_nrd_eq.lean

